window.__DATA_walkthrough = {"meta":{"schema":"designer-matrix/walkthrough.json v2 \u2014 layer 3, rows the study did not evaluate","purpose":"Apply the framework from outside the study to languages that were not part of it, and feed the result back through the same tool.","languages":["unison"],"count":1,"classification":"computed at query time by QUERY.place from patterns.json family_rule \u2014 never stored here","note":"Every verdict must come from a probe that was built and run. A null verdict means not yet measured, and never a guess."},"languages":[{"language":"unison","meta":{"schema":"designer-matrix/unison.json v1 \u2014 layer 3, a row the study did not evaluate","language":"unison","purpose":"The walkthrough: apply the framework from outside the study to a 45th language, and feed the result back through the same tool.","toolchain":{"installed_via":"brew install unisonlang","binary":"ucm","version":"1.4.0","checked":true,"note":"ucm version prints \"unknown (built on )\"; the Homebrew formula version is the pin"},"module_construct":"namespace \u2014 a hierarchical name prefix in a project's codebase, with `lib.*` as the dependency subtree","evaluated":true,"scored":20,"of":20,"bypass_attempted":8,"bypass_possible_not_written":0,"bypass_no_prohibition_cells":3,"generated":"2026-09-29T03:48:36Z","runs":33,"note":"Every verdict here comes from a probe that was built and run. A null verdict means not yet measured, and never a guess. Verdicts are PROPOSED and await author validation; bypass routes are the author's to rule.","source":"fse/section5/unison-probes/unison-evaluation.json"},"cells":[{"language":"unison","property":"P01","property_name":"Information hiding","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N1 (by convention only); not N2; not N3","partial_route":"concealment is conventional \u2014 a member may be *named* internal and the name is listed beside the surface; ordinary access succeeds","enforcement_type":"none","violation_outcome":"accepted","violation_phase":"n/a","support_origin":"conventional","granularity":"none \u2014 no per-member visibility exists","language_specific_construct":"namespace-name-convention","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P01","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"Unison has no access modifier. The intended-internal member is reached directly (21) and the constructor field is read directly (7). The codebase does enforce one rule over the dependency subtree \u2014 a scratch file may not MODIFY anything under `lib` \u2014 but reading a transitive dependency by full path succeeds (99), and N2 concerns naming and reading.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P02","property_name":"Interface typing","support":"full","support_conditions":"N1; N2; N3; N4 (all)","partial_route":"n/a","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"rejected","violation_phase":"compile","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"record-of-operations","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P02","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"A record type is an interface artefact distinct from any implementation of it, clients are checked against the record type, and a field of the wrong type is refused at typecheck: \"has type: Nat but I expected: Text\".","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P03","property_name":"Module-level parameterisation","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N1; N3; N4; not N2","partial_route":"parameterisation reaches only definitions within a namespace \u2014 the namespace itself cannot be abstracted over a parameter or applied to an argument","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"n/a","violation_phase":"compile","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"parametric-definition","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P03","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"An ordinary definition abstracts over a parameter and runs at two different arguments (42, \"hi!!\"), and a record of operations gives a declared constraint whose non-conforming argument is rejected. But a namespace is a name prefix: no form abstracts one over a parameter, so N2 fails and the unit parameterised is never the module.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P04","property_name":"Separate compilation","support":"full","support_conditions":"N1; N2; N3 (all) \u2014 by a mechanism the condition did not anticipate","partial_route":"n/a","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"rejected","violation_phase":"compile","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"content-addressed-definition","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P04","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"Unison has NO link step and no interface artefact, and yet the skew N3 exists to catch cannot occur: a dependent names a specific hash, so changing a definition produces a different hash and `update` refuses \u2014 \"I couldn't complete the update, because some existing definitions would no longer typecheck\" \u2014 handing back the affected dependents. The skew window is eliminated rather than checked, which is a design no language in the 44 uses. Phase is recorded, not scored (R4): detection is at change time, earlier than link.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P05","property_name":"Type abstraction","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N1; N2; not N3; not N4","partial_route":"the representation is recoverable by ordinary means \u2014 a data constructor is always nameable, so pattern matching extracts the underlying value","enforcement_type":"none","violation_outcome":"accepted","violation_phase":"n/a","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"unique-type-constructor","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P05","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"`unique type` gives a nominal type whose name can be exported, and clients can operate through the exported operations (\"$42\"). But the constructor cannot be withheld: the violation pattern-matches it and recovers the Nat (42). This is criteria.md's partial route (a) exactly \u2014 representation recoverable by ordinary means.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P06","property_name":"Module composition","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N1; N2; not N3","partial_route":"composition flattens \u2014 a member a constituent intended to withhold is reachable through the composite, because nothing was concealed to begin with","enforcement_type":"none","violation_outcome":"n/a","violation_phase":"n/a","support_origin":"tool-mediated","granularity":"none \u2014 no per-member visibility exists","language_specific_construct":"namespace-copy","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P06","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"`copy.namespace` composes two namespaces under a common prefix and the result is itself a namespace, so composition is closed. But it is a codebase command, not a language form, and the composite exposes the constituents' intended internals: the client reaches Combined.a.internal.helper (42).","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P07","property_name":"Namespace management","support":"full","support_conditions":"N1; N2; N3 (all)","partial_route":"n/a","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"n/a","violation_phase":"compile","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"hierarchical-name-prefix","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P07","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"Two namespaces export `size` with neither in error, a client uses both by qualification (3), and the unqualified name is REFUSED as ambiguous rather than silently shadowed \u2014 which is N3's discriminating condition.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P08","property_name":"Required interfaces","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N1; N2; N3; N4 for abilities \u2014 not for definition dependencies","partial_route":"requirements are declared and typed for **abilities**, which appear in the signature; requirements on other definitions are **inferred from the body** and never declared","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"rejected","violation_phase":"compile","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"ability-in-signature","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P08","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"An ability in a type signature is a genuine typed requirement in the declared surface, determinable without reading the body, and an unmet one is refused: \"needs the {Store} ability, but this location does not have access to any abilities\". A caller that handles it is accepted. But which other definitions a module requires is inferred from its body, which is criteria.md's partial route (b) \u2014 so the property splits by what kind of requirement is at stake.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P09","property_name":"Higher-order parameterisation","support":"absent","support_conditions":"not N1 \u2014 there is no module-level parameterisation to be higher-order over","partial_route":"n/a","enforcement_type":"n/a","violation_outcome":"n/a","violation_phase":"n/a","support_origin":"n/a","granularity":"n/a","language_specific_construct":"n/a","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P09","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"P09 depends on P03's N2, which fails: a namespace cannot be abstracted over a parameter, so no parameterised module exists to take or return one. Higher-order FUNCTIONS work to any depth (42), which is P03's partial route carried up a level and not evidence for this property.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P10","property_name":"Authority control","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N1; N3; N4; not N2","partial_route":"a custom ability is mediated by a handler, but `IO` is reachable by any definition that names an IO builtin, and a written signature that omits an ability is silently widened rather than refused","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"accepted","violation_phase":"compile","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"ability-handler","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P10","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"Abilities are a real capability mechanism: a value needing {Store} with no handler is refused, and a handler grants it. But TWO findings cut against N2. A declared ability set is not a constraint \u2014 `declaredPure : Nat -> Nat` calling an {IO} definition is accepted and RECORDED as `Nat ->{IO} Nat`, so a programmer cannot declare that a definition must not reach a capability. And `unsafe.coerceAbilities` discards the requirement: the coerced definition TYPECHECKS and is added, then fails at run time with \"unhandled ability request\" \u2014 the boundary falls as a typing judgement while the value never crosses, which is the shape the corpus already records for coq's axiom route.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P11","property_name":"Versioning","support":"full","support_conditions":"N1; N2; N3; N4 (all) \u2014 identity is the content hash","partial_route":"n/a","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"rejected","violation_phase":"compile","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"content-hash-identity","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P11","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"A definition's identity is its content hash and the codebase reports it: #t7g50rohbm before the change, #o9l28uhum9 after. The substitution rule is applied in-language and mechanically \u2014 an incompatible replacement is refused by `update` before any combination. This is the STRONGEST claim in the walkthrough and the one most in need of author validation: the identity is a content hash rather than a declared version, and the rule is exact-identity plus dependents-still-typecheck, so there is no notion inside the language of a compatible-but-different version.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P12","property_name":"Hierarchical nesting","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N1; N2; N3; not N4","partial_route":"nesting reaches any depth and members are reachable by path, but hiding does not survive the path because no hiding exists","enforcement_type":"none","violation_outcome":"n/a","violation_phase":"n/a","support_origin":"native","granularity":"none \u2014 no per-member visibility exists","language_specific_construct":"hierarchical-name-prefix","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P12","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"Depth three works and the nested member is reached by explicit path (7). N4 fails for the same reason P01 is only conventional: the inner intended-internal member is reached by naming its full path (13).","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P13","property_name":"Dependency structure","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N2; N3; N4; N1 only in part \u2014 the graph is inspectable but never declared","partial_route":"the graph is inferred from each definition's body rather than declared, while remaining fully inspectable and validated before anything runs","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"rejected","violation_phase":"compile","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"inferred-hash-graph","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P13","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"The graph is inspectable in both directions \u2014 `dependencies` and `dependents` both answer \u2014 and a missing dependency is refused at typecheck, before anything runs. What Unison does not have is an explicit DECLARATION of dependencies: the graph is inferred from the free names in each body. N1 asks for both, so the cell records the half that holds and names the half that does not.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P14","property_name":"Mutual recursion","support":"full","support_conditions":"N1; N2; N3; N4 (all)","partial_route":"n/a","enforcement_type":"n/a","violation_outcome":"n/a","violation_phase":"n/a","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"hash-cycle","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P14","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"`Even.isEven` and `Odd.isOdd` live in different namespaces and call each other. The cycle is accepted with no forward declaration, no laziness annotation and no mutable cell, and both namespaces keep their own names.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P15","property_name":"First-class modules","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N1; N2; N3 hold for a record of operations \u2014 not for the namespace","partial_route":"modules are values only by wrapping the operations in a record; a namespace has no expression form and cannot be bound, passed or returned","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"n/a","violation_phase":"n/a","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"record-of-operations","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P15","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"A record of operations is bound, passed, returned, selected on run-time data and keeps its type \u2014 \"doubling -> 42\" and \"incrementing -> 22\" from the same call site. All three conditions hold of the record. None holds of the namespace, which has no expression form at all. Scored `partial` on the same reading as P19: the thing that is first-class is a wrapper, not the module construct.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P16","property_name":"Dynamic module loading","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N2; N3 for identity only \u2014 not for interface; not N4","partial_route":"the loaded unit is a serialised **term**, not the namespace; and the load checks identity but not interface \u2014 `Value.load`'s result type is fixed by the calling context rather than verified against the bytes","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"rejected","violation_phase":"runtime","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"value-serialise-load","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P16","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"`Value.serialize` then `Value.deserialize` and `Value.load` bring a term into a running program \u2014 \"loaded and ran: 42\" \u2014 and loading IS checked: corrupt bytes are refused (\"rejected at load: insufficient bytes in getWord32be\") and missing dependencies come back as `Left [Term]`, checked by hash rather than by name. What is loaded is a term, so N4 fails: the deployment unit is not the namespace.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P17","property_name":"Access-control granularity","support":"absent","support_conditions":"not N1 \u2014 selection rests on naming discipline alone","partial_route":"n/a","enforcement_type":"none","violation_outcome":"accepted","violation_phase":"n/a","support_origin":"n/a","granularity":"none \u2014 no per-member visibility exists","language_specific_construct":"n/a","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P17","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"`ls Svc` lists every member, and the client calls the one intended to be withheld (42). There is no qualified-export form, no per-client visibility and no re-export control, so there is no gradation to be finer than binary \u2014 the binary distinction itself does not exist. This is criteria.md's `absent` verbatim: selection rests on naming discipline alone.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P18","property_name":"Generative modules","support":"absent","support_conditions":"not N1 \u2014 no module-level instantiation exists","partial_route":"n/a","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"n/a","violation_phase":"compile","support_origin":"n/a","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"unique-type-declaration","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P18","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"A namespace cannot be applied to an argument, so there is nothing to instantiate generatively. The nearest analogue does exist and is mechanically enforced: `unique type` gives fresh nominal identity per DECLARATION, and confusing two such types is refused (\"but I expected: Meters\"). Freshness keyed to a declaration is not two instantiations of one parameterised module at equal arguments.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P20","property_name":"Applicative modules","support":"absent","support_conditions":"not N1 \u2014 no module-level instantiation exists","partial_route":"n/a","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"n/a","violation_phase":"n/a","support_origin":"n/a","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"structural-type-declaration","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P20","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"As P18: no module instantiation exists. The analogue is sharper here \u2014 two separately declared `structural type`s with the same structure collapse to ONE identity, \"#v7h0ofmeja Type BoxA, BoxB\", and a value built with one constructor is consumed by the other's accessor (42). So Unison exhibits BOTH the generative and the applicative distinction, keyed to whether a type is declared `unique` or `structural` \u2014 and neither is keyed to instantiating a module.","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"},{"language":"unison","property":"P19","property_name":"Multiple module instances","support":"partial","support_conditions":"N2; N3; not N1 at module granularity","partial_route":"instances are reachable only by wrapping the state in another construct \u2014 a definition returning a fresh `Ref` \u2014 so it is the wrapper, not the namespace, that is multiply instantiated","enforcement_type":"mechanical","violation_outcome":"rejected","violation_phase":"compile","support_origin":"native","granularity":"declaration","language_specific_construct":"ref-per-call","evidence_source":"executable","evidence_completeness":"complete","bypass_outcome":"n/a","probe":{"cmd":"see unison-probes/P19","executed":true,"outcome":"pass","exit":0,"status":"executed"},"finding":"Two `Ref`s from the same definition keep separate state \u2014 (1, 2, 1) \u2014 and the isolation needs no arrangement by the programmer. But a namespace cannot be instantiated at all, which is criteria.md's partial route (b).","verdict_status":"proposed-pending-author-validation"}]}]};
